# 1. Purpose and Scope

This document specifies the functional requirements for the Reporting module of the OPEX Budgeting System (OBS). It defines the business rules, data rules, access control behaviors, report definitions, and acceptance criteria that govern report viewing, variance analysis, version and year comparison, variance annotations, saved filters, and Excel export.

This specification resolves the following open items from the Project Context Handoff v2.4:

- Reporting — fixed templates vs. user-configurable reports.

- Reporting — saved views.

- Reporting — variance annotations and commentary.

- Reporting — historical version comparison.

## 1.1 In Scope

- Report List page — display of published report types and report authoring access for Report Developers and Administrators.

- Report viewer — filter panel, data grid, drill-down, variance color coding, and ‘Data as of’ and ‘Budget last set’ timestamps.

- Report type definitions — two initial report types: Annual Budget Summary and Budget by Month.

- Column and row visibility control — user-managed within published report type column sets.

- Comparison mode — version-to-version comparison (within or across fiscal years) and year-over-year actuals comparison.

- Variance annotations — written notes added per row by users with ALL_WRITE standard grant, visible to all users with access to the cost center.

- Saved filters — personal, named filter sets persisted across sessions; unlimited per user.

- Excel export — server-side, respecting confidential data grants and visible column selection.

- Audit events for all reporting actions that constitute data mutations (annotation create/update/delete, saved filter create/update/delete, Excel export).

- PostgreSQL schema additions required by this specification.

- API endpoint requirements for all of the above.

## 1.2 Out of Scope

- Report definition authoring UI — the full interaction design is specified in UX and UI Specification v1.5 Section 7.6, which resolved OI-RPT-01.

- Finance-side approval workflow — fully specified in Functional Requirements: Finance Approval Workflow v1.2.

- In-application notification mechanism — fully specified in In-Application Notification Mechanism Specification v1.1.

- Ad-hoc query building — users may not construct arbitrary queries or define new report types.

