All open items are now resolved. No outstanding items remain in this specification.

**Resolved in v1.0:** The following open items from Project Context Handoff v2.3 were resolved by the v1.0 specification:

| **Item** | **Resolution** |
| --- | --- |
| Reporting — fixed templates vs. user-configurable reports | Resolved. Reports are fixed types published by Report Developers. Users may control column visibility and row visibility within the available column set of the published report type. Users may not create ad-hoc queries or define new report types. |
| Reporting — saved views | Resolved. Users may save named filter sets (saved filters) that persist across sessions. Saved filters are personal. No limit on saved filters per user. See Section 10. |
| Reporting — variance annotations and commentary | Resolved. Users with ALL_WRITE standard grant on a cost center may add written annotations to specific report rows. Budget Planning module commentary is read-only in the Reporting module. Annotations and commentary are separate fields. See Section 9. |
| Reporting — historical version comparison | Resolved. Users may compare two budget versions side by side (within or across fiscal years) and may compare current year actuals or budget against prior year actuals. See Section 6.1.5. |

# 15. Acceptance Criteria

Each criterion below must be verified by automated test or documented manual test procedure before the Reporting module is considered complete. Criteria from UX and UI Specification v1.5 Sections 7.5 and 7.6 (AC-UP-RPT-01 through AC-UP-RPT-09 and AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-01 through AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-18) remain in force and are not repeated here — this section adds the functional and data-layer criteria.

## 15.1 Access Control

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-RPT-AC-01** | An Administrator receives report data for all cost centers without any cost center grant. |
| **AC-RPT-AC-02** | A Report Developer receives report data for all cost centers regardless of cost center grants. |
| **AC-RPT-AC-03** | A System Modeler receives report data for all cost centers regardless of cost center grants. |
| **AC-RPT-AC-04** | A user with only ALL_READ standard grant on one cost center receives report data for that cost center only. Requests for other cost centers return HTTP 403. |
| **AC-RPT-AC-05** | Compensation columns are absent from API responses for cost centers where the requesting user holds ALL_NONE confidential data grant — fields are absent from the payload, not null. |
| **AC-RPT-AC-06** | Excel export excludes compensation columns for cost centers where the exporting user holds ALL_NONE confidential data grant. |
| **AC-RPT-AC-07** | Annotation write attempts by a user with ALL_READ standard grant (and no Administrator flag) return HTTP 403. |
| **AC-RPT-AC-08** | Saved filter read operations return only the authenticated user's own saved filters — never another user's. |
| **AC-RPT-AC-09** | Saved filter write and delete operations on a filter_id belonging to a different user return HTTP 403. |

## 15.2 Report Viewer and Filters

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-RPT-VW-01** | The report data grid displays all rows and columns matching the current filter panel state. Changes to filters do not take effect until the user clicks 'Apply'. |
| **AC-RPT-VW-02** | The 'Reset to defaults' link restores all filter panel controls to their default values. |
| **AC-RPT-VW-03** | Selecting a rollup node in the cost center filter includes all child cost centers in the report. Adding a new cost center under that rollup is automatically included on next report load. |
| **AC-RPT-VW-04** | The row visibility filter restricts visible account rows to the selected set. Account hierarchy group rows reflect only the selected children, not the total of all children. |
| **AC-RPT-VW-05** | Grouping by quarter produces four column groups (Q1–Q4) each containing the sum of their constituent monthly budget and actuals amounts. |
| **AC-RPT-VW-06** | Grouping by half-year produces two column groups (H1, H2). Grouping by year produces one annual total column. |
| **AC-RPT-VW-07** | The 'Data as of' timestamp is returned by /api/v1/reporting/data-currency and refreshed on every report data load. It is never cached from a prior session. |
| **AC-RPT-VW-08** | The 'Budget last set' timestamp is returned per cost center in the report API response and reflects the latest updated_at across all budget lines for that cost center, fiscal year, and version. |
| **AC-RPT-VW-09** | All variance values displayed in the grid match the server-returned values — the frontend does not independently derive variance calculations. |
| **AC-RPT-VW-10** | All rollup and aggregate row values are computed server-side and match the sum of their constituent rows. |
| **AC-RPT-VW-11** | Attempting to apply a row visibility filter that would produce zero visible rows returns HTTP 422. |

## 15.3 Comparison Mode

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-RPT-CM-01** | When version comparison mode is active, the report shows budget amounts for both the primary and secondary versions as separate columns, plus a variance column showing primary minus secondary. |
| **AC-RPT-CM-02** | Version comparison supports selecting versions from different fiscal years. The secondary version's fiscal year is independent of the primary fiscal year filter. |
| **AC-RPT-CM-03** | When prior-year actuals comparison mode is active with sub-option 'current year actuals vs. prior year actuals', the report shows both actuals datasets and their variance. |
| **AC-RPT-CM-04** | When prior-year actuals comparison mode is active with sub-option 'current year budget vs. prior year actuals', the report shows the primary version budget alongside prior year actuals and their variance. |
| **AC-RPT-CM-05** | Both sub-options may be selected simultaneously, producing all four data columns (current actuals, prior actuals, current budget, prior actuals) plus both variance columns. |
| **AC-RPT-CM-06** | Comparison mode may be combined with any grouping selection (month, quarter, half-year, year). |

## 15.4 Annual Budget Summary Report

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-RPT-ABS-01** | The Annual Budget Summary report displays one row per leaf-level expense account visible to the user, plus account hierarchy group rows aggregating child accounts. |
| **AC-RPT-ABS-02** | The Forecast column reflects the budget version the user has designated as the forecast in the filter panel — not a system-level designation. |
| **AC-RPT-ABS-03** | Selecting multiple fiscal years produces separate budget, target, forecast, and prior-year columns for each year, with fiscal year indicated in the column header. |
| **AC-RPT-ABS-04** | A maximum of 5 fiscal years may be selected simultaneously. Requests for more than 5 fiscal years return HTTP 422. |
| **AC-RPT-ABS-05** | If no active version exists for a prior fiscal year, the prior-year budget column for that year is blank (null) and variance columns referencing it are null. |
| **AC-RPT-ABS-06** | Variance percentage columns display null (blank) when the denominator is zero or null. |

## 15.5 Budget by Month Report

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-RPT-BBM-01** | The Budget by Month report displays one period column per planning period (1–12) when grouped by month. Column headers display abbreviated month name and year. |
| **AC-RPT-BBM-02** | The Total Budget, Budget Target, and Current Year Budget summary columns always reflect the full fiscal year total regardless of the grouping selection. |
| **AC-RPT-BBM-03** | The Current Year Budget column always reflects the active version for the selected fiscal year, not the user's selected primary version. When they are the same version, the Vs. CY Budget variance is zero. |
| **AC-RPT-BBM-04** | If no active version exists for the selected fiscal year, the Current Year Budget column is blank and Vs. CY Budget variance columns are null. |
| **AC-RPT-BBM-05** | Selecting a cost center rollup node in the cost center filter produces rollup rows aggregating all child cost center amounts. Drill-down into individual cost centers is available from rollup rows. |
| **AC-RPT-BBM-06** | Selecting an account hierarchy group in the row visibility filter shows the group row and all selected child accounts. The group row reflects only selected children. |

## 15.6 Variance Annotations

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-RPT-AN-01** | An annotation created on a row context (cost_center_id + account_code + fiscal_year + version_id) is visible in both the Annual Budget Summary and Budget by Month report for that row context. |
| **AC-RPT-AN-02** | Creating a second annotation on the same row context updates the existing annotation — no duplicate annotation rows are created. |
| **AC-RPT-AN-03** | Annotation text exceeding 1,000 characters is rejected with HTTP 422. |
| **AC-RPT-AN-04** | Deleting an annotation sets annotation_text = null and generates a REPORT_ANNOTATION_DELETED audit event. The obs.report_annotations row is retained. |
| **AC-RPT-AN-05** | Budget Planning module commentary (obs.budget_lines.commentary) is returned as a read-only field in report API responses and is not writable via any Reporting module endpoint. |
| **AC-RPT-AN-06** | Users with ALL_READ standard grant see annotation text as read-only. The edit icon is not displayed for these users. |

## 15.7 Saved Filters

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-RPT-SF-01** | A saved filter created by user A is not returned in any API call made by user B. |
| **AC-RPT-SF-02** | A user may create an unlimited number of saved filters. No quota error is returned regardless of saved filter count. |
| **AC-RPT-SF-03** | Creating a saved filter with a name that already exists for the same user returns HTTP 409. |
| **AC-RPT-SF-04** | A saved filter name exceeding 100 characters is rejected with HTTP 422. |
| **AC-RPT-SF-05** | Applying a saved filter that references a budget version that is now Archived substitutes the active version and displays a warning message to the user. |
| **AC-RPT-SF-06** | Applying a saved filter that references an unpublished report type displays a warning and does not load the report. |
| **AC-RPT-SF-07** | Restoring a saved filter populates all filter panel controls with the saved state. The user must explicitly click 'Apply' to reload the report data. |

## 15.8 Excel Export

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-RPT-EX-01** | The Excel export includes all visible rows and all visible columns matching the current filter state at the time of export. |
| **AC-RPT-EX-02** | Compensation columns are absent from the export for cost centers where the exporting user holds ALL_NONE confidential data grant. |
| **AC-RPT-EX-03** | The export file name follows the pattern: {report_name}_{cost_center_name}_{fiscal_year}_{YYYYMMDD}.xlsx. |
| **AC-RPT-EX-04** | The export includes a summary block above the data grid containing the 'Actuals data as of' and 'Budget last set' timestamps. |
| **AC-RPT-EX-05** | A REPORT_EXPORTED audit event is generated for every export, capturing user_id, report_definition_id, cost_center_ids, fiscal_year, version_id, column_count, row_count, file_name, and exported_at. |
| **AC-RPT-EX-06** | A single cost center export completes within 10 seconds from API request to file availability. |

